  $vtg$krog$vtg$, $vtg$atlanta$vtg$, $vtg$Krog Street Tunnel$vtg$, $vtg$Street art$vtg$, array[$vtg$Street$vtg$]::text[], $vtg$blue$vtg$, $vtg$Neon and spray paint after dark$vtg$, $vtg$Ever-changing murals · night color$vtg$, $vtg$A quarter-mile of layered graffiti that repaints itself weekly. As blue hour settles, the tunnel lights turn the walls electric and the color balance falls right into place.$vtg$, array[$vtg$Fresh paste-ups near the east mouth change every few days.$vtg$, $vtg$Long exposures blur passing cyclists into ribbons of light.$vtg$, $vtg$Puddles after rain double the color underfoot.$vtg$]::text[], $vtg$9 min drive · park at Krog Street Market · tunnel is a 2-min walk north.$vtg$, null, 33.754, -84.362, true)
